        "explanation": "I didn't change anything in `hmr.ts`. The one issue is left for review.\n\n**Issue 1 (line 323, `TODO Trigger their dispose callbacks.`):** The TODO is still accurate. `prunePaths` (`hmr.ts:324`) runs only the prune callbacks. It never calls the dispose callbacks in `this.disposeMap` for the modules it prunes, so there's no finished work to justify deleting the note. Rewording it to dodge the rule would just hide the problem, which the rules don't allow.\n\nDoing what the TODO asks would change runtime behavior. `prunePaths` would also need to call `this.disposeMap.get(path)?.(this.dataMap.get(path))` for each path before its prune callback. Dispose callbacks can return a Promise, so done properly the method would become `async` and return `Promise<void>`. Every caller of `prunePaths` would then need to `await` it. That's a deliberate feature change across files, so it's not something to make just to clear a lint warning.\n\nTo resolve it, either implement dispose-on-prune (making `prunePaths` async and updating its callers), or move the TODO into an issue tracker and remove the comment."
      },
